{
  "_readme": [
    "Route classification for the Brazn Tasks managed edition (BRA-925).",
    "",
    "Every mutating API route (anything that is not a plain read) must appear",
    "here exactly once, classified as one of:",
    "",
    "  protected-topology - creates, moves, renames or deletes a project or a",
    "                       team. These can touch the structures the product",
    "                       guarantees: each member's Inbox, the organization's",
    "                       Public root and each team's root.",
    "  access-expanding   - shares a project, invites or adds a member, grants",
    "                       a right, creates a link share, makes something",
    "                       public, or can move a task out of a private Inbox",
    "                       into a shared project. Routes that manage the",
    "                       access surface in either direction belong here.",
    "  ordinary           - normal task work that continues under stock",
    "                       Vikunja permissions and needs no managed-mode",
    "                       check.",
    "",
    "TestMutatingRoutesAreClassified in route_classification_test.go derives",
    "the real route list from RegisterRoutes at test time and fails CI when a",
    "mutating route is missing here or an entry here no longer exists. Method",
    "ANY is echo's catch-all used by the CalDAV handlers. GET/HEAD/OPTIONS and",
    "the read-only WebDAV methods are presumed non-mutating by contract; a GET",
    "that changes state would not be caught here and must never be added.",
    "",
    "Keep entries sorted by path, then method (byte order) - the test enforces",
    "this so parallel additions merge cleanly.",
    "",
    "Since BRA-914 this file is also the managed-mode policy table, not only a",
    "record. Every protected-topology and access-expanding entry carries a",
    "\"managed\" rule name, and RequireManagedPolicy looks the request up here at",
    "runtime; TestGuardedRoutesCarryAManagedRule fails CI when one is missing.",
    "A rule the running build has no decision for denies the request - unmapped",
    "means deny, never skip - so a newly classified route is closed by default",
    "until its policy is written.",
    "",
    "Rules:",
    "  disabled         - the managed edition does not offer this at all; the",
    "                     route answers 404, like an unregistered one.",
    "  service-managed  - performed by Brazn's commercial service, never by a",
    "                     customer request.",
    "  authentication   - signing in is never gated by managed mode; see",
    "                     managed_rules_core.go for why.",
    "  access-revoke    - revoking access never expands it, so it stays open,",
    "                     except on the protected roots themselves.",
    "  everything else  - an edition-specific policy: project-create,",
    "                     project-duplicate, project-update, project-delete,",
    "                     project-share, link-share, teams-only, task-move.",
    "",
    "A few ordinary routes also carry \"disabled\" - API token, CalDAV token and",
    "bot provisioning. Those are feature switches, not policy checks. An",
    "ordinary route may carry no other rule: normal task work must keep working",
    "even when the commercial service cannot be reached.",
    "",
    "POST /api/v1/brazn/entitlements is classified \"ordinary\" with no rule, and",
    "it is the one entry where that word is read in its operative sense - \"not",
    "gated by managed mode\" - rather than its descriptive one. It is not task",
    "work. It is the door the commercial service delivers a signed entitlement",
    "projection through (BRA-913), and the three classes have no member for a",
    "service-plane route.",
    "",
    "The alternatives were considered and are wrong, not merely less tidy. Both",
    "guarded classes require a \"managed\" rule, and every rule that exists either",
    "refuses outright - \"service-managed\" refuses everything, which would 403",
    "the service this route exists for - or resolves an acting user and reads",
    "their entitlement first, which deadlocks: the endpoint that writes the",
    "first projection cannot require one to run. The endpoint is also called by",
    "no user at all, so the gate could not resolve an acting user even if a rule",
    "wanted one.",
    "",
    "What actually guards it is stronger than a class: it authenticates the",
    "signed message against the keys in brazn.entitlementkeys, and that trust",
    "store is empty by default. The rule that an ordinary route carries no",
    "policy check is exactly right here for the same reason it is right for task",
    "work - the door the entitlement arrives through must not be gated on the",
    "entitlement it delivers.",
    "",
    "A fourth class (\"service-plane\") would say this more honestly and is worth",
    "considering the next time one of these appears. One route did not justify",
    "widening a vocabulary two harnesses and the enforcement path all read.",
    "",
    "POST /api/v1/brazn/provisioning is \"ordinary\" with no rule for exactly the",
    "same reasons, and it is the second of these rather than the second kind of",
    "them: it is the door the commercial service creates a Brazn Tasks user",
    "through (BRA-1018), authenticated by the same Ed25519 signature against the",
    "same trust store, and it has no acting user either. Every sentence above",
    "about why neither guarded class fits applies to it unchanged - most",
    "sharply the deadlock one, because this is the endpoint that creates the",
    "user an entitlement is later addressed to, so requiring one to run is",
    "requiring the account to exist before it is made.",
    "",
    "It is deliberately ONE entry for every provisioning operation. The",
    "operation is a value inside the signed payload rather than a path, so",
    "BRA-1026's organization roots arrive through this route and this entry.",
    "That is the point of the shape: a second service-plane path would have to",
    "argue its classification again, and an argument made three times is one",
    "somebody eventually makes differently.",
    "",
    "Two of these now exist, which is the condition the note above set for",
    "reconsidering a \"service-plane\" class. It is still not taken here: the",
    "channel design means the count stops at two however many operations the",
    "commercial service gains, so the vocabulary would be widened for a set that",
    "is no longer growing."
  ],
